Golden per-candidate capture for the Rust portfolio port (RUST-PLAN.md section 1,
native/PORT-SPEC.md sections 6-7).

Gated on TS_GOLDEN_DUMP=<path>; zero behavior change when unset. Hooks
PortfolioSingleIntraNodeSolver.parallelReplayStep immediately after
runReplayRace() returns — the one point where EVERY candidate (all classes:
CachedIntraNodeRouteSolver variants, A01/A03, polyline, closed-form, adaptive
A01 expansions) has run TO COMPLETION with final routes, iterations and full
progress trajectories, and the deterministic replay winner is known. Same
completion point, flag pattern and lazy-require discipline as the proven
RPLYDS01 hook (native/replay-core/capture-hook.patch, now committed).

Adds one file, native/replay-core/goldenDump.ts (the JSONL sink; per-100-
iteration trajectories via datasetFormat.decimateTrajectory, bit-exact on the
schedule grid), plus a 17-line hook. Output is JSON-lines: one "board" line
(obstacles/layerCount, once), one "node" line per node (shared input:
nodeWithPortPoints, scalar params, connMap slice — per-candidate input is too
big to inline per line, and shared-input + hp fully determines a candidate),
then one "cand" line per candidate {nodeId, i, hp, solved, iterations,
maxIterations, solvedSegments, routes, error, traj}.

Capture runbook (mirrors native/replay-core/README.md step 4; do NOT run while
the benchmark gauntlet holds the box):

    env -u TS_PARALLEL_REPLAY2 -u TS_PARALLEL_HD_NODES -u TS_PARALLEL_A2 \
      -u TS_LEAN_PORTFOLIO \
      TS_PARALLEL_PORTFOLIO=1 TS_PARALLEL_REPLAY=4 \
      TS_GOLDEN_DUMP=/abs/path/srj18-sample8.golden.jsonl \
      bun scripts/run-sample.ts --pipeline 7 --sample 8 --dataset srj18

Apply from the worktree root:   git apply native/golden-capture.patch
Revert:                        git apply -R native/golden-capture.patch

